<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Microphone. Two keys, because macOS checks different ones depending on
      how the app is signed and hardened:

        com.apple.security.device.audio-input
          The Hardened Runtime key. On macOS 26 this is the one checked before
          the app is allowed to appear under Privacy & Security > Microphone.
          Without it a hardened app can silently never receive the prompt.

        com.apple.security.device.microphone
          The App Sandbox flavour. Inert for us (we are not sandboxed) but
          harmless, and it costs nothing to be correct under both regimes.

      App Sandbox is deliberately absent: a system-wide CGEventTap and
      Accessibility-based text injection are incompatible with it (ADR-011).

      Anything added to this file widens the TCC/privilege surface and must be
      justified in TECH_DECISIONS.md first.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.microphone</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
